happen. So let's say it did happen. What can we do to bring ourselves back to square one, right? And just putting those fears under the microscope and putting practical ways forward in the case to avoid it in the first case, but then in the case of actually happening, how do we move ourselves back? It's a really, really good way to break down those fears and it allows us to have a road map to move forward and then we could just get on and do it without that fear holding us back. What about parents and other caregivers? What can they do to encourage their kids while buffering them from the pressures that lead to perfectionism? I mean, you know you want your kid to get into the best school, but how can you keep your child from becoming overly anxious and suffering?
会发生什么。所以假设它确实发生了。我们能做些什么来让自己回到原点，对吧？把这些恐惧放在显微镜下，在第一种情况下采取实际的前进方式来避免它，但在实际发生的情况下，我们如何让自己回到原点？这是一种非常非常好的打破这些恐惧的方法，它让我们有了一个前进的路线图，然后我们就可以继续做下去，而不会让那种恐惧阻碍我们。父母和其他照顾者呢？他们能做些什么来鼓励他们的孩子，同时缓冲他们免受导致完美主义的压力？我的意思是，你知道你希望你的孩子进入最好的学校，但你如何防止你的孩子变得过度焦虑和受苦？

