people have done, well, they've come home, they've got an A in their test, and and you go, that's great, okay, keep working, right? Because that full approval, full validation and recognition of parents is subtly withheld under the understanding of more. So essentially what we're doing is we're holding young people on tiptoes under the expectation they keep working. And that teaches them that they're only really worth something in this world if they strive and strive and strive and strive. And if they achieve and achieve and the moment they don't, then the implication is that other people will value them less. So conditional forms of acceptance are really problematic when it comes to development of perfectionism.
人们做到了，嗯，他们回家了，考试得了A，然后你会说，太棒了，好吧，继续努力，对吧？因为那种完全的赞许、完全的认可和肯定，在“更多”的理解下被微妙地克制了。所以本质上，我们所做的是让年轻人踮着脚尖，期待他们不断努力。这教会他们，只有在不断奋斗、奋斗、再奋斗的过程中，他们在这个世界上才真正有价值。如果他们不断取得成就，而一旦没有做到，那么言下之意就是别人会降低对他们的评价。因此，当涉及到完美主义的发展时，这种有条件的接受方式是非常成问题的。

